WEBVTT

00:28:28.900 --> 00:28:30.473
This is the doctor talking.

00:28:30.497 --> 00:28:32.443
"We need to talk about quitting smoking.

00:28:32.467 --> 00:28:35.718
We talked about this last time
and there hasn't been much progress."

00:28:35.742 --> 00:28:40.006
Patient: "It's been really hard
since my mom died."

00:28:40.030 --> 00:28:42.616
Doctor: "Well, if you don't quit,

00:28:42.640 --> 00:28:44.656
you're going to have another heart attack

00:28:44.680 --> 00:28:47.644
and you're going to get that lung
cancer you're worried about."

00:28:47.668 --> 00:28:48.703
(Adam groans)

00:28:48.727 --> 00:28:51.226
AB: How did that one feel for you?
AG: Horrible.

00:28:51.250 --> 00:28:54.216
AB: So the issue, though, is,

00:28:54.240 --> 00:28:56.986
if you dissect that with the clinician

00:28:57.010 --> 00:28:58.211
and you were to say,

00:28:58.235 --> 00:29:00.976
"OK, let's just pause
that conversation for a second.